      "type": "authorbook-hello",
      "settings": {
        "eyebrow": "About",
        "heading": "Ten years of <em>twenty pages</em> a day",
        "text": "<p>I grew up in a house with more books than shelves, and for most of my twenties I hardly read any of them. I worked long days, read the news on my phone and bought books I meant to start on holiday.</p><p>Then I tried something smaller: twenty pages before bed, and one page of notes when a book was done. A decade later I have read more than four hundred books and still remember most of them. Write your own story here.</p>",
